><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Hansen</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Alper</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Inheritable variable sizes of DNA stretches in human MHC: conserved extended haplotypes and their fragments or blocks</article-title><source>Tissue Antigens</source><year>2003</year><volume>62</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>20</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12859592</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1034/j.1399-0039.2003.00098.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sj&#x000f6;wall</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Carlsson</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Vaarala</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Bergstrom</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Ernerudh</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Forsberg</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Ekerfelt</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Innate immune responses in Lyme borreliosis: enhanced tumor necrosis factor-alpha and interleukin-12 in asymptomatic individuals in response to live spirochetes</article-title><source>Clin Exp Immunol</source><year>2005</year><volume>141</volume><fpage>89</fpage><lpage>98</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15958074</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1365-2249.2005.02820.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Blum</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Cork</surname><given-names>LC</given-names></name><name><surname>Morris</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Olson</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Winkelstein</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></per